{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include <algorithm>\\n#include <iostream>\\n#include <utility>\\n#include <vector>\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\\n\\nint main() {\\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\\n\\n    int n, m;\\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\\n\\n    vector<pair<int, int>> blocked;\\n    blocked.reserve(static_cast<size_t>(m));\\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\\n        int row, column;\\n        cin >> row >> column;\\n        blocked.emplace_back(row + column, row);\\n    }\\n    sort(blocked.begin(), blocked.end());\\n    blocked.erase(unique(blocked.begin(), blocked.end()), blocked.end());\\n\\n    vector<int> previous(n, 0);\\n    vector<int> current(n, 0);\\n    size_t blockedIndex = 0;\\n\\n    auto updateFreeRange = [&](int begin, int end, int diagonal) {\\n        if (begin < end && begin == 0) {\\n            current[0] = previous[0];\\n            ++begin;\\n        }\\n\\n        int vectorBegin = max(begin, 1);\\n        int vectorEnd = min(end, diagonal);\\n        // Rows in this span read only the previous diagonal and write distinct cells.\\n        #pragma GCC ivdep\\n        for (int row = vectorBegin; row < vectorEnd; ++row) {\\n            int sum = previous[row] + previous[row - 1];\\n            if (sum >= MOD) sum -= MOD;\\n            current[row] = sum;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (diagonal < n && begin <= diagonal && diagonal < end) {\\n            current[diagonal] = previous[diagonal - 1];\\n        }\\n    };\\n\\n    for (int diagonal = 0; diagonal <= 2 * n - 2; ++diagonal) {\\n        while (blockedIndex < blocked.size() && blocked[blockedIndex].first < diagonal) {\\n            ++blockedIndex;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (diagonal == 0) {\\n            if (blockedIndex < blocked.size() && blocked[blockedIndex].first == 0) {\\n                current[0] = 0;\\n                ++blockedIndex;\\n            } else {\\n                current[0] = 1;\\n            }\\n            previous.swap(current);\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n\\n        int lowRow = max(0, diagonal - (n - 1));\\n        int highRow = min(n - 1, diagonal);\\n        int rowCursor = lowRow;\\n\\n        while (blockedIndex < blocked.size() && blocked[blockedIndex].first == diagonal) {\\n            int blockedRow = blocked[blockedIndex].second;\\n            updateFreeRange(rowCursor, blockedRow, diagonal);\\n            current[blockedRow] = 0;\\n            rowCursor = blockedRow + 1;\\n            ++blockedIndex;\\n        }\\n        updateFreeRange(rowCursor, highRow + 1, diagonal);\\n\\n        previous.swap(current);\\n    }\\n\\n    cout << previous[n - 1] << '\\\\n';\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/solution.cpp\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Traversing the grid by anti-diagonals removes the row-wise loop-carried dependency: cells on one diagonal depend only on the preceding diagonal. The free-cell interiors can therefore be legally exposed to GCC SIMD vectorization while retaining O(N) DP storage and the same O(N²) work.\",\"notes\":\"The SIMD pragma applies only to spans whose iterations read the separate previous-diagonal buffer and write distinct current cells. Blocked cells split spans and are set to zero; duplicate obstacles are removed. The controller should evaluate correctness and speed.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Replace the in-place left-to-right row recurrence with a two-buffer anti-diagonal recurrence, preserving blocked-cell and endpoint semantics.\",\"Sort and deduplicate obstacles by diagonal and row so each diagonal can be processed in contiguous free spans.\",\"Use GCC ivdep on the dependency-free interior of each free span; handle diagonal boundary cells separately.\"]}"}}
